.SH NAME
niac-simulation-forget - Forget a saved scenario that failed to restart


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBniac simulation forget  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Delete a saved scenario the daemon could not restore after a restart, for example because its interface is unplugged, so it is no longer retried at every restart. Needs an admin-scoped token. A scenario that is running is stopped with 'simulation stop', not forgotten.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for forget


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--api\fP=""
	Daemon API address (default: https://127.0.0.1:8445, or NIAC_API_URL)

.PP
\fB--cacert\fP=""
	Daemon certificate to trust (default: the local daemon's own, when visible)

.PP
\fB--insecure\fP[=false]
	Skip TLS verification, for a daemon whose certificate this host cannot see

.PP
\fB--storage-keep\fP=500
	Run history records to keep, pruned oldest first on start (0 keeps every run)

.PP
\fB--storage-path\fP=""
	Path to NIAC run history database (default: ~/.niac/niac.db)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  niac simulation forget modern
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBniac-simulation(1)\fP


